//! Caravan recant -- a judgment a run's own evidence disproves is taken back on
//! the wire and repaired, rather than carried forward because it was written
//! down first.
//!
//! `appraise.rye` taught a plan to publish the standard by which its silences
//! are read, and a run to weigh an unmarked loss by what came home after it.
//! That judgment goes to the wire, and it stays there: a judgment outlives the
//! run that made it, which is exactly what makes it a record. Yet the evidence
//! under it belongs to one run alone. A later run of the same plan meets that
//! standing judgment with evidence of its own, and nothing below this rung ever
//! asks the two to agree.
//!
//! **The measurement is arcs spared on a judgment this run's own evidence
//! disproves.** The rung below weighs judgment: work a run did that its author
//! never spoke to and that nobody needed. This one weighs the **honesty of a
//! judgment over time** -- work a run declined to do on the word of a run that
//! is over, while its own record says that word no longer holds. A plan comes
//! out settled under the elder reading, and it settles `borne` -- which tells an
//! operator there is nothing left to do, while an arc of the plan stands unserved.
//!
//! **A plan publishes whether its own judgments may be weighed again.** A record
//! written `review = .revisit` says: a standing appraisal answers to the evidence
//! of every run that meets it. `review = .stand` is where the rung below leaves
//! it -- a judgment once published stands, and a run that meets it adds its own
//! rather than weighing it. The word sits at the plan beside the standard,
//! since it is an instruction about how a record's own history should be read.
//!
//! **The standing appraisal is the one note a run does not clear.** Every other
//! note a plan carries is provisioned back to nothing at the head of a run, so
//! no supervisor reads the last run's word as its own. The appraisal is left
//! exactly where it was, because a judgment that vanished with its run was never
//! a record -- and because this rung's whole subject is what a run does with a
//! judgment it did not make.
//!
//! **A recantation is bounded by the judgment it takes back.** Only an arc a
//! standing appraisal named may be recanted, and every standing judgment this
//! run can weigh is upheld or recanted -- never both and never neither. A run
//! that recanted an arc nobody spared would be inventing a reversal, which is
//! the same overreach as repairing work the wire never named.
//!
//! **The recantation stands on the wire beside the appraisal it reverses.** One
//! glyph per phase, `r` where a standing judgment was taken back, so `.r....`
//! names which phase of six this run refused to spare on an older run's word --
//! written while the run still holds the evidence, and read back before the
//! repair seats a single phase on its strength.
//!
//! **The rung earns four refusals, and each is about the reversal rather than
//! the repair it opens.** `RecantEarly` is the moment: a standing judgment
//! weighed again before this run published what *it* lost is judging from
//! memory. `RecantUnappraised` is the supply: a recantation reaching an arc no
//! appraisal ever spared has taken back a judgment nobody made. `RecantMiscounted`
//! is the honesty of the count: every standing judgment is upheld or recanted,
//! and never two of those and never none. `RecantUnspoken` is the answer -- the
//! hard half -- since a run that recanted an arc and then declined to repair it,
//! or that published a settlement the wire's own recantation does not support,
//! would report a reversal it never carried out.
//!
//! **A plan the wire holds no judgment about reads as the rung below.** With no
//! standing appraisal to meet, the reversal is refused before it weighs
//! anything, each line stands at the width it was handed, and the door answers
//! `unhand.admissible_held` pair for pair -- this arc's standing generalization
//! test, one tier further out.
//!
//! Usage:
//!   recant            Run the self-test (default)
//!   recant selftest   Same as default
//!   recant dependent ...  Run as one supervised dependent (spawned by the run)
const std = @import("std");
const assert = std.debug.assert;
const print = std.debug.print;
const system = @import("system.rye");
const capabilities = @import("capabilities.rye");
const roster = @import("roster.rye");
const read = @import("read.rye");
const boot = @import("boot.rye");
const exercise = @import("exercise.rye");
const carry = @import("carry.rye");
const notify = @import("notify.rye");
const roundtrip = @import("roundtrip.rye");
const cycle = @import("cycle.rye");
const regions = @import("regions.rye");
pub const queue_store = @import("queue.rye");
pub const serve = @import("serve.rye");
const gap = @import("gap.rye");
const cohort = @import("cohort.rye");
const intent = @import("intent.rye");
const mask = @import("mask.rye");
const precede = @import("precede.rye");
const overtake = @import("overtake.rye");
const unhand = @import("unhand.rye");
const entrust = @import("entrust.rye");
const confer = @import("confer.rye");
pub const revoke_rung = @import("revoke.rye");
const reclaim_rung = @import("reclaim.rye");
const abandon_rung = @import("abandon.rye");
const bearing_rung = @import("bear.rye");
const appraising_rung = @import("appraise.rye");
const mending_rung = @import("mend.rye");
const tally_parse_int = @import("parse_int.rye");
const ladder_checks = @import("ladder_checks.rye");

const Dir = std.Io.Dir;

const caravan_recant_version = "20260820.042716";

// =========================================================================
// The bounds -- carried whole from the rung below, with the reclaiming's own
// =========================================================================

/// The declaration this rung runs over, unchanged.
pub const declaration_path = appraising_rung.declaration_path;

/// How many dependents one supervisor holds at once.
pub const max_in_flight: u32 = appraising_rung.max_in_flight;

/// How many phases one record may hold.
pub const max_queue_len: u32 = appraising_rung.max_queue_len;

/// How far past a blocked head a run may look for a phase that may pass.
pub const max_lookahead: u32 = appraising_rung.max_lookahead;

/// How many words a dependent receives before its capability words begin.
pub const fixed_argv_words: u32 = appraising_rung.fixed_argv_words;

/// How many turns one plan may name.
pub const max_turns: u32 = appraising_rung.max_turns;

/// Where the reckoning notes live, kept apart from every other rung's.
pub const note_dir = "caravan/.recants";

/// The longest note path this rung ever writes.
pub const max_note_path_len: u32 = appraising_rung.max_note_path_len;

/// The longest capability word this wire carries, from the spawn's own bound.
pub const max_word_bytes: u32 = appraising_rung.max_word_bytes;

/// The longest word list one dependent is ever handed, one word per line.
pub const max_words_bytes: u32 = appraising_rung.max_words_bytes;

/// How long a look rests before looking again.
pub const note_rest_ms: u32 = appraising_rung.note_rest_ms;

/// How many times a supervisor looks for a dependent's answer before refusing.
pub const max_confirm_looks: u32 = appraising_rung.max_confirm_looks;

/// How many times a dependent looks for more reach before it comes home.
pub const max_patience_looks: u32 = appraising_rung.max_patience_looks;

/// How many times a dependent looks for a pruning before it comes home.
pub const max_prune_looks: u32 = appraising_rung.max_prune_looks;

comptime {
    // invariant: a run always has a slot to remember a live dependent's line by
    assert(max_in_flight >= 1);
    // invariant: an abandoned word list still fits the wire that carries it
    assert(max_words_bytes >= max_word_bytes + 1);
    // invariant: a note path leaves room for the directory and a name
    assert(max_note_path_len > note_dir.len + regions.max_name_len);
    // invariant: this rung's notes never collide with the appraising notes
    assert(!std.mem.eql(u8, note_dir, appraising_rung.note_dir));
    // invariant: this rung's notes never collide with the reclaiming notes
    assert(!std.mem.eql(u8, note_dir, reclaim_rung.note_dir));
    // invariant: this rung's notes never collide with the revoking notes
    assert(!std.mem.eql(u8, note_dir, revoke_rung.note_dir));
    // invariant: this rung's notes never collide with the conferring notes
    assert(!std.mem.eql(u8, note_dir, confer.note_dir));
    // invariant: a dependent always has room to look for the reach it is owed
    assert(max_patience_looks >= 1);
}

// =========================================================================
// The shapes -- carried whole from the rung below
// =========================================================================

/// Renders one outcome code as the words an operator reads.
pub fn outcome_name(code: u8) []const u8 {
    return appraising_rung.outcome_name(code);
}

/// Why a queue may not take, correct, understudy, unhand, taper, entrust,
/// confer, revoke, reclaim, answer for its work, claim it is done, repair it,
/// carry the loss its author asked it to bear, weigh the loss its author left
/// unmarked, or take back a judgment its own evidence disproves.
///
/// Four names of this rung's own, and each is about the reversal rather than
/// the repair it opens: the moment a standing judgment is weighed again, the
/// supply it may reach, the honesty of the count, and the reversal it publishes
/// once the repair is over.
pub const RunError = appraising_rung.RunError || error{
    RecantEarly,
    RecantUnappraised,
    RecantMiscounted,
    RecantUnspoken,
};

/// One queued item and the letters it declares, carried from `intent.rye`.
pub const Task = appraising_rung.Task;

/// How deeply a reading looks at the queue's own authorship, unchanged.
pub const Reading = appraising_rung.Reading;

/// One phase, its turn, its step, its masks, the reserve it may be entrusted,
/// and the bearing its author may write beside it.
///
/// This rung adds no word here either, and for the same reason the rung below
/// added none: what it weighs is a judgment made about a phase rather than
/// anything the phase's author wrote. Whether a record's own judgments answer
/// to a later run's evidence is a statement about the whole record, so it lives
/// at the plan beside the standard.
pub const Phase = struct {
    turn: u32 = 0,
    step: u32 = 0,
    follows: u32 = 0,
    follows_turns: u32 = 0,
    reserve: ?Task = null,
    bear: bool = false,
    task: Task,
};

/// The phase as the rung below reads it, bearing and all, since the rung below
/// already knows that word and this one adds none.
pub fn below(phase: Phase) appraising_rung.Phase {
    // invariant: a phase always names the domain its author wrote
    assert(phase.task.item.domain.len >= 1);
    return .{
        .turn = phase.turn,
        .step = phase.step,
        .follows = phase.follows,
        .follows_turns = phase.follows_turns,
        .reserve = phase.reserve,
        .bear = phase.bear,
        .task = phase.task,
    };
}

/// The phase as the rungs below read it, without the reserve they never had.
pub fn plain(phase: Phase) unhand.Phase {
    return appraising_rung.plain(below(phase));
}

/// When a dependent comes to hold the arcs of its reserve, from the rung below.
pub const Reach = appraising_rung.Reach;

/// What becomes of a conferred word while its holder still stands.
pub const Keep = appraising_rung.Keep;

/// One bounded word list, exactly as the conferring wire renders it.
pub const Words = appraising_rung.Words;

/// What a run says its plan came to, carried whole from the rung below.
pub const Verdict = appraising_rung.Verdict;

/// Renders one verdict as the words an operator reads.
pub fn verdict_words(v: Verdict) []const u8 {
    return appraising_rung.verdict_words(v);
}

/// The one byte a verdict rides as, so an operator's note is a single glyph.
pub fn verdict_byte(v: Verdict) u8 {
    return appraising_rung.verdict_byte(v);
}

/// Reads one verdict back from the byte it rode as, or nothing at all.
pub fn verdict_of_byte(byte: u8) ?Verdict {
    return appraising_rung.verdict_of_byte(byte);
}

/// Answers why one reckoning may not be taken, or that it may.
pub fn reckon_refusal(absorbed: u32, in_flight: u32, lost: u32) ?RunError {
    return appraising_rung.reckon_refusal(absorbed, in_flight, lost);
}

/// Counts the completion a run claimed that its own work does not support.
pub fn overclaimed_completion(lost: u32, verdict: Verdict) u32 {
    return appraising_rung.overclaimed_completion(lost, verdict);
}

/// How a run decides whether its plan was carried out, from the rung below.
///
/// This rung settles that question rather than reopening it: every run here
/// reckons, because a mend that repaired a plan under the assuming reading
/// would be repairing a loss it had already declared did not matter.
pub const Ledger = appraising_rung.Ledger;

/// Renders one ledger as the words an operator reads.
pub fn ledger_words(l: Ledger) []const u8 {
    return appraising_rung.ledger_words(l);
}

/// Answers what a plan came to, under one ledger.
pub fn verdict_in(lost: u32, ledger: Ledger) Verdict {
    return appraising_rung.verdict_in(lost, ledger);
}

/// What one run did, reported whole, with the reversal it made added.
///
/// `spared_disproved` is the number this rung moves: arcs a run declined to
/// repair on the word of a standing appraisal, while its own record says that
/// word no longer holds. `recanted` is what it took back instead, published on
/// the wire and repaired.
pub const Report = struct {
    inner: appraising_rung.Report = .{},
    recanted: u32 = 0,
    spared_disproved: u32 = 0,
};

/// This rung's own recanting tally, reached by the same name the rungs above
/// reach it by.
///
/// Every rung above this one finds the recantation through `recanting_of`,
/// climbing a nesting of `inner` to arrive here. This rung *is* that tier, so
/// the reach is the report itself -- and naming it anyway is what lets the one
/// body every rung of this arc runs stand byte for byte in this rung too,
/// rather than nearly. An accessor born for the tier a rung owns costs three
/// lines and folds a hundred and seventy-eight (fold J's lesson, once more).
pub fn recanting_of(report_out: *Report) *Report {
    return report_out;
}

/// The appraising rung's own tally, which this one wraps.
///
/// Every rung of this arc wraps the report of the rung below it, so one named
/// reach per tier keeps the supervisor readable and keeps a miscount from
/// hiding inside a chain of `inner`.
pub fn appraising_of(report_out: *Report) *appraising_rung.Report {
    return &report_out.inner;
}

/// The bearing rung's tally, one tier further down.
pub fn bearing_of(report_out: *Report) *bearing_rung.Report {
    return &report_out.inner.inner;
}

/// The mending rung's tally, two tiers further down.
pub fn below_of(report_out: *Report) *mending_rung.Report {
    return &report_out.inner.inner.inner;
}

/// The abandoning rung's tally, five tiers further down.
pub fn abandoning_of(report_out: *Report) *abandon_rung.Report {
    return &report_out.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner;
}

/// The run's own tally, reached without spelling the whole nesting each time.
pub fn run_of(report_out: *Report) *overtake.Report {
    return &report_out.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.run;
}

/// The sibling-order counters, reached the same way.
pub fn masked_of(report_out: *Report) *mask.Report {
    return &report_out.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner;
}

/// The turn-order counters, reached the same way.
pub fn preceded_of(report_out: *Report) *precede.Report {
    return &report_out.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner.inner;
}

/// The single bit that stands for one turn of a plan.
pub fn turn_bit(turn: u32) u32 {
    return appraising_rung.turn_bit(turn);
}

/// Answers whether the plan's written sequence keeps every name it carries.
pub fn plan_is_seated(plan: []const unhand.Phase) bool {
    return appraising_rung.plan_is_seated(plan);
}

/// Answers whether two phases must keep the order the queue wrote them in.
pub fn items_contend(sys: *const system.System, a: unhand.Phase, b: unhand.Phase, reading: Reading) bool {
    return appraising_rung.items_contend(sys, a, b, reading);
}

/// Counts the arcs one line names.
pub fn hop_count(task: Task) u32 {
    return appraising_rung.hop_count(task);
}

/// Counts the arcs a reserve offers, or zero where a phase named none.
pub fn reserve_depth(reserve: ?Task) u32 {
    return appraising_rung.reserve_depth(reserve);
}

